{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"tools":{}},"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","serverInfo":{"name":"hilo-mcp","version":"0.4.1"}}}
{"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"tools":[{"description":"Read Hilo extended attributes for a file.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"keys":{"description":"Optional xattr short-name filter (e.g. ['feature', 'risk'])","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_get_metadata"},{"description":"Set a Hilo extended attribute on a file.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"key":{"description":"Attribute name (e.g., 'feature', 'risk', 'purpose')","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file","type":"string"},"value":{"description":"Attribute value to set","type":"string"}},"required":["path","key","value"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_set_metadata"},{"description":"Find files related to the given file via the dependency graph. Supports forward (outgoing) and reverse (incoming) queries.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"direction":{"description":"Query direction: 'forward' (outgoing, default) or 'reverse' (incoming)","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"File path to find related files for","type":"string"},"relation":{"description":"Filter by relation type (e.g. 'imports', 'tested_by', 'tests')","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_related"},{"description":"Get summary statistics about the dependency graph.","inputSchema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_stats"},{"description":"List files that have import edges but no test coverage (no tested_by edges).","inputSchema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_untested"},{"description":"Get per-module file listing and test coverage statistics from the dependency graph.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"module_name":{"description":"Directory prefix to query (e.g., 'src/auth/')","type":"string"}},"required":["module_name"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_module"},{"description":"Find all files that depend on the given file, directly or transitively.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"max_depth":{"description":"Maximum traversal depth (default: 5)","type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"File path to compute impact for","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_impact"},{"description":"Get harmonic multi-resolution context for a task — MAP (file→symbols), SIGNATURES (one-line per symbol), DETAIL (whitespace-minified source). Position-ordered, budget-controlled, deterministic. Definitions that name the task are always listed; `local:` import specifiers are resolved to the file they name.\n\nANCHORING IS LITERAL: task words are matched against file paths and symbol names, so the task text IS the query. Name the subsystem plus what it does, in 3-6 concrete words.\n\nGood task descriptions (every word names something in the tree):\n- \"trigger debounce middleware\" → the debounce engine and its trigger config\n- \"parse edges duckdb\" → the graph parser and the DuckDB store\n- \"workspace mount preflight\" → the mount preflight path\n\nToo vague:\n- \"workspace\", \"config\", \"auth\" → a single generic word matches weakly, so the map comes back thin and unfocused\n\nIf the MAP looks thin, or the output says nothing anchored: do NOT retry the same words. Add the subsystem and the action (\"fuse workspace mount preflight\", \"debounce should_fire per file\") and call again. The no-anchor output names the subsystems this repository actually has; vfs_graph_search is the keyword-sweep fallback.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"budget":{"description":"Token budget (default: 6000)","type":"integer"},"resolution":{"description":"Output mode: 'harmonic' (3-tier, default) or 'flat' (single-tier)","type":"string"},"task":{"description":"Natural-language task description — 3-6 words naming the subsystem and what it does (e.g. 'trigger debounce middleware'), not a single generic word (e.g. 'workspace')","type":"string"}},"required":["task"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_understand"},{"description":"Semantic code search using TF-IDF + BM25 + Reciprocal Rank Fusion. Finds files by meaning, not just literal text matches. Deterministic, no external API calls.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Max results to return (default: 20)","type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"Search query (e.g. 'authentication middleware', 'rate limiter')","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_search"},{"description":"COV-5 symbol-level connection + test audit. Per public function, answers whether it is reachable from a declared entrypoint and whether it carries a test link, and returns the NAMED list partitioned into three buckets — unreachable (no caller path from an entrypoint), unlinked (reachable, no test link), ok (reachable AND linked) — each with a count and the rule that produced it. Languages without a public-function extractor are named under `unknown` rather than counted as ok. Pure source analysis: needs no warmed graph.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Optional project root to audit (defaults to the server's working directory)","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_graph_audit"},{"description":"List all rules defined in the Hilo manifest (stale-files, untested-critical, transitive-impact, etc.).","inputSchema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_rule_list"},{"description":"Execute a named rule query against the dependency graph and return matching files.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"name":{"description":"Name of the rule to execute (e.g., 'stale-files')","type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_rule_check"},{"description":"List entries in a virtual directory: backends mount table entries first, then the real local filesystem when the virtual listing is empty. Empty result means an empty directory; nonexistent paths and file paths return an error.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Virtual directory path to list","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_list_directory"},{"description":"Resolve a virtual path to its real storage location.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Virtual path to resolve","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_resolve_path"},{"description":"Get backend information for a file — which backend owns it, cache status, remote URL, and last sync state.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"File path to query backend status for","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_backend_status"},{"description":"Sync the backend for a file — returns count of synced files and any errors. Ignored/ephemeral paths are local-only and report skipped_ignored instead of transferring.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"File path to sync the backend for","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_sync_backend"},{"description":"List ephemeral (rebuildable/redownloadable) files in the workspace — path, size, and the deciding rule. Defaults to the workspace root; an optional path limits the listing to that subtree.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Optional path limiting the listing to a subtree","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_workspace_ephemeral"},{"description":"Plan or apply a wipe of ephemeral files. dry_run defaults to true (planned only); pass dry_run=false to delete. The response echoes the resolved mode as dry_run. Files with user.vfs.ephemeral=false are never removed. removed_count is the total number of matched entries; removed[] carries at most the first 200 entries and removed_truncated is true when it was cut off.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"dry_run":{"description":"When true (default) only plan; when false, delete","type":"boolean"},"path":{"description":"Optional path limiting the wipe to a subtree","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"vfs_workspace_wipe"}]}}
